15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting a data analysis process that starts with raw data, followed by data cleaning, branching into four groups with clinical, test, and ultrasound data, each leading to separate models. A detailed blue section illustrates feature selection and further subgroup divisions, including ungrouped, body mass index less than twenty-four, body mass index greater than or equal to twenty-four, regular, and irregular cycle groups, each leading to their own models.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Four horizontal bar charts display the feature correlation with PCOS \(Y/N\) for subgroup 1, subgroup 2, subgroup 3, and ungrouped datasets. Each chart lists features such as skin darkening, hair growth, weight gain, BMI, and other clinical variables, ordered by their correlation with PCOS status, with subgroup 3 and ungrouped charts containing additional features compared to subgroup 1 and subgroup 2. Positive and negative correlation values are shown, indicating the relative importance of features across groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a data processing framework for PCOS diagnosis, beginning with user input of clinical, test, and ultrasound data, followed by processing and structuring, application of subgroup and ungrouped models, and resulting in outputs of PCOS classification, risk score, and risk analysis, with integration of a PCOS knowledge base and an AI assistant named Lingshu.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Screenshot of two medical report interfaces from AutoPCOS showing risk analysis for polycystic ovary syndrome \(PCOS\). The first report for a non-PCOS participant shows a risk score of 3.1 percent, highlighting normal clinical and morphological features, and a horizontal bar chart with negative and minor positive feature contributions. The second report for a PCOS participant shows a risk score of 95.2 percent, with prominent indicators such as high follicle numbers and clinical signs, and a horizontal bar chart with large positive feature contributions confirming potential PCOS.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
